# What restore-first-catalog.sh holds the two dumps to (k8s plan 0012, section 1).
# A shell file that the script sources. A checksum that differs is refused by
# restore-database.sh before a scratch database exists, and a count that differs
# is a refusal, not a warning.
#
# The values below are the checksums and counts of the dumps of
# 2026-10-07T10:28:17Z (2026-10-07 12:28 Madrid time). They were taken after
# two data stages of that day: the re-file of 2,250 products onto the leaves of
# backend plan 0179, and the second curation walk, which created 2,430 products
# from queue rows that the first walk could not place. Only the gateway was
# served, and it holds no database, so nothing wrote. They replace the values
# of the dumps of 2026-10-06T23:32:21Z, which held neither stage.
#
# These dumps are the ones that ship, unless slot 1 is written again. A later
# write means new dumps and new values here (README.md, "When slot 1 is
# final"). The owner has NOT yet said that slot 1 is final. The copy that the
# owner restored onto the owner's own machine on 2026-10-07 is older: it is the
# restore of the dumps of 2026-10-06T22:33:14Z, and it holds neither stage.
# The two files are NOT uploaded to a bucket yet. A file with other bytes is
# refused at the checksum, which is the intended failure.
#
# The object keys, under a prefix that the nightly dumps never use.
CATALOG_KEY="imports/2026-10-first-catalog/catalog.dump"
CATALOG_SHA256="f81e6023528d17f6b6e457a8e27a216ecb388d43883a0b9b9c145c9d92a04880"
HARVESTER_KEY="imports/2026-10-first-catalog/harvester.dump"
HARVESTER_SHA256="e75f10e693304f357060e3dc42d8c68c8cbf18ae09dbde830f975ed256d20f08"
#
# The `migrations` table of each dump: how many rows, and the name with the
# highest timestamp. The live database must hold the same names.
CATALOG_LAST_MIGRATION="ItemEans1758800000000"
CATALOG_MIGRATIONS="29"
HARVESTER_LAST_MIGRATION="SourceEntryPriceKind1759200000000"
HARVESTER_MIGRATIONS="21"
#
# The state in numbers (apps/luna-shopper-backend/docs/initial-catalog-2026-10.md).
EXPECT_SUPERMARKETS="5"
EXPECT_PRICE_SCOPES="105"
EXPECT_CATEGORIES="309"
EXPECT_BRANDS="2830"
EXPECT_ITEMS="22203"
EXPECT_ITEM_PRICES="25074"
EXPECT_SOURCE_ENTRIES="25861"
EXPECT_SOURCE_ENTRIES_ACTIVE="24223"
